<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugo Oct trade gap $192 mln vs $130 mln in Sept.</title>
<headline>Yugo Oct trade gap $192 mln vs $130 mln in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV TRADE	(OCT 96)    (SEPT 96)	   (OCT 95)</p>
<p> Exports million USD	155	  154			n.a</p>
<p> Imports		  347	  284			n.a.</p>
<p> Balance		 -192	 -130			n.a.</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE FIGURES (JANUARY TO OCT 1996)</p>
<p> Exports million USD    1,425	1,259			n.a.</p>
<p> Imports		3,131	2,655			n.a.</p>
<p> Balance	     -1,706     -1,396			n.a.</p>
<p>NOTES -- Data refers to Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>Comparative figures for the previous year are not available as the country was under an international trade embargo which was lifted on October 1 after nearly four and a half years.</p>
<p>-- Gordana Filipovic, Belgrade newsroom, +381 11 222 4254</p>
